---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";

const scaffoldCode = [
  `<span class="cm"># scaffold a new game project (after the npm release lands)</span>`,
  `<span class="fn">pnpm</span> create g2w my-game`,
  ``,
  `<span class="kw">cd</span> my-game`,
  `<span class="fn">pnpm</span> install`,
  `<span class="fn">pnpm</span> dev`,
].join("\n");

const addCode = [
  `<span class="fn">pnpm</span> add @g2w/core @g2w/runtime @g2w/renderer-pixi @g2w/input-dom`,
  `<span class="fn">pnpm</span> add pixi.js <span class="cm"># renderer-pixi peer: PixiJS 8</span>`,
].join("\n");

const treeCode = [
  `my-game/`,
  `├── index.html            <span class="cm"># #game canvas + #error box</span>`,
  `├── package.json          <span class="cm"># dev / build / test scripts</span>`,
  `├── tsconfig.json`,
  `├── src/`,
  `│   ├── main.ts           <span class="cm"># composition root</span>`,
  `│   └── scenes/`,
  `│       └── play-scene.ts <span class="cm"># pure game logic</span>`,
  `└── test/`,
  `    └── play-scene.test.ts <span class="cm"># deterministic, no browser</span>`,
].join("\n");
---

<Base title="Installation · g2w docs">
  <div class="docs">
    <DocsSidebar active="installation" />

    <main class="docs-main prose">
      <div class="crumb">docs / getting-started / installation</div>
      <h1>Installation</h1>
      <p>
        g2w is a set of small npm packages composed at the application boundary. The
        fastest path is the <code>create-g2w</code> CLI, which scaffolds a complete
        TypeScript + Vite game project from a bundled template.
      </p>

      <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
      <p>
        <b>Node.js ≥ 22</b> and a package manager. Every g2w package is ESM-only with
        <code>NodeNext</code> resolution, and the scaffolded project uses Vite for dev
        serving and bundling. pnpm is recommended but npm, yarn, and bun all work.
      </p>

      <h2 id="scaffold">Scaffold with create-g2w</h2>
      <p>
        The CLI never prompts and runs no shell commands; its only subprocess is a
        local <code>git init</code> in the generated directory (skipped when Git is
        missing or the destination already has Git metadata).
      </p>
      <div class="codeblock" style="box-shadow: none">
        <div class="cb-head"><span>shell</span></div>
        <pre><code set:html={scaffoldCode} /></pre>
      </div>
      <p>
        The generated project ships with a playable scene — a square you steer with
        WASD or the arrow keys — wired through <code>G2WGame</code>, a
        <code>SceneManager</code>, and a unit-tested movement module:
      </p>
      <div class="codeblock" style="box-shadow: none">
        <div class="cb-head"><span>project structure</span></div>
        <pre><code set:html={treeCode} /></pre>
      </div>

      <h2 id="manual">Manual setup</h2>
      <p>
        Prefer to wire things yourself? Install the packages you need and follow
        <a href="/docs/your-first-game">Your First Game</a>:
      </p>
      <div class="codeblock" style="box-shadow: none">
        <div class="cb-head"><span>shell</span></div>
        <pre><code set:html={addCode} /></pre>
      </div>
      <p>
        <code>@g2w/core</code> is the only package with zero runtime dependencies.
        <code>@g2w/renderer-pixi</code> adapts PixiJS 8 to the renderer contract, and
        <code>@g2w/runtime</code> adds the Effect-based <code>G2WGame</code>
        lifecycle. Add <code>@g2w/input-gamepad</code> for gamepads,
        <code>@g2w/audio-web</code> for sound, and <code>@g2w/devtools</code> for the
        read-only dev overlay.
      </p>

      <h2>Honest status</h2>
      <div class="callout" style="box-shadow: none">
        <span class="tag">Status</span>
        <span>
          <b>All @g2w/* packages are published to npm at 0.1.0</b> (released
          2026-10-28 via OIDC trusted publishing). This is an early 0.x release:
          the public API may still change before 1.0. The scaffolded project
          pins <code>@g2w/*</code> at the released version.
        </span>
      </div>

      <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
      <p>
        Head to <a href="/docs/your-first-game">Your First Game</a> to walk through
        the scaffolded project line by line, or read the
        <a href="https://github.com/AlexanderDev2004/g2w/blob/main/docs/architecture.md"
          >architecture notes</a
        > for the boundary rules behind the package split.
      </p>
    </main>

    <aside class="docs-toc">
      <div class="ttl">On this page</div>
      <a class="on" href="#">Installation</a>
      <a href="#requirements">Requirements</a>
      <a href="#scaffold">Scaffold with create-g2w</a>
      <a href="#manual">Manual setup</a>
      <a href="#next">Next steps</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
